# world.fk: your base, one plot: 2000x2000 tiles (nauvis.fk places it; 2000,2000 here is the map
# corner at 999,999, so a map tile x,y is this file's x+1000, y+1000).
#
# The reactor and its pole line (plant.fk) and the starter kit the kickoff puts down (kit.fk) stand
# inside this plot from the start, as the world's own furniture: the design declares them, so they
# are yours to build around, extend or take up. Everything else you add here is your base.
#
# Build each factory as a sealed module: `module NAME size WxH { ... }` with `port` lines on its
# edges. Its own belts stay inside its frame; the belts between factories are nets written here,
# from one factory's port to the next one's. A change inside one factory never moves another.
#   docs\LANGUAGE.md "Modules with ports"   the module, its ports, its contract
#   docs\EXAMPLES.md busbase.fk             a whole base built this way: smelting, a bus,
#                                          circuits, a mall and science
# Two items into one row share a belt, a lane each: `lanes A | B` (the build's could-pair check names
# the pair when you leave them on two belts).
# A factory used in several places (or a big one) can live in a file of its own:
#   import Smelting from "smelting.fk"
import Plant from "plant.fk"
import Kit from "kit.fk"
import FurnacePair, CopperPair, GearCell, CircuitCell, RedCell2, GreenCell, LabCell3, AdvCircuitCell2, EngineCell, ChemCell2 from "cells.fk"
import SteelCell from "steelcell.fk"
import LabArea from "labarea.fk"
import BeltMall2 from "beltmall.fk"

plant = Plant @(966, 961)      # the reactor and its poles, at map -34,-39
kit   = Kit @(1000, 1000)      # the kit: chests, roboport, panels, accumulators, poles at map 0,0

# ---- A0 (10-31, scaffolding first: Rory "build scaffolding and modularity early") ----
# BACKBONE: a pinned roboport grid, 48 apart so the logistic areas overlap into one network, off
# the ore; construction (+-55) covers coal, stone, copper and iron. Never moved by a route.
#   G1/G2 (Rory 10-31: links are square, L-inf; ore in the corners of the grid, roboports on
#   free ground): kit (8,8); r1 (-12,26) -> r3 (-14,74); r2 (50,26) -> r4 (36,74).
#   All four moved in one paste (~101k): every new spot is in the kit's or new r1/r2's reach.
r1 = Roboport @(988, 1026)    # G1 (Rory 10-31: shift ~20 W, 30 N); ~585k a plain roboport again (the auto mall moved to the kit roboport)
r2 = Roboport @(1050, 1026)   # G1: was 56,56 (x 50, not 36: cl_cl at x72 stays in its logistic square)
r3 = Roboport @(986, 1076)    # G1: was 6,104; ~196k 2 S: fe_pl4's first belt (8.5,130.5) was 54.5 out, past reach
r4 = Roboport @(1036, 1074)   # G1: was 56,104
r5 = Roboport @(1048, 960)    # R2 (~1334k): map 50,-38, inside the kit roboport's reach (r0 @45,-55 was out of every construction area, so never built); covers R1 east
e1 = Roboport @(1098, 962)   # E1 (~2150k, Rory: this base is the starter; the real base goes east): corridor east along map y -38
e2 = Roboport @(1148, 962)   # E1: 50 apart so the logistic squares touch
e3 = Roboport @(1198, 962)   # E2 (~2240k)
e4 = Roboport @(1248, 962)   # E2: ~70 from the spitter spawners at map 300..314, 14..26
e5 = Roboport @(1263, 978)   # E3a (~2290k): map 265,-20: construction reach x210..320, y-75..35 covers the 3 spitter spawners (300..314, 14..26) for the mine wave; ~49 from the nearest
e6 = Roboport @(1313, 1008)  # U0 corridor (~2370k): map 315,10 (L-inf <= 50 from e5)
e7 = Roboport @(1363, 1043)  # map 365,45
e8 = Roboport @(1408, 1083)  # map 410,85: its logistic square 385..435, 60..110 holds u0
e9 = Roboport @(1363, 978)    # E4 (~2770k): map 365,-20 (L-inf 50 from e6): the chain toward the nest cluster at x480..497, y-46..-35
e10 = Roboport @(1413, 958)   # E4: map 415,-40
e11 = Roboport @(1443, 960)   # E4: map 445,-38: construction reach x390..500 covers the cluster for mine wave 2 (35 from the nearest spawner)
e12 = Roboport @(1493, 938)   # E5 (~2835k): map 495,-60, W of the 7M iron (x520..568, y-100..-44; wave 2 cleared its nests)
e13 = Roboport @(1493, 888)   # E5: map 495,-110
e14 = Roboport @(1543, 888)   # E5: map 545,-110, between the iron and the copper (x520..560, y-172..-124); off the ore
e15 = Roboport @(1493, 838)   # E6b (~2925k): map 495,-160: cu2_col reaches y-170, past e13/e14's construction reach (y-165): 26 ghosts sat uncovered
u0 = Literal<file="captured/u0.json"> @(1424, 1100)   # lab-built uranium trigger outpost (FRICTION: MinerRow takes no fluid)

# boot (map 12..28, -8..1), the hub seed by the kit's roboport. A0: gears -> belts (the fields
# need 253, the kit has 200) and stone furnaces, from the kit's plates and stone. B: cable,
# circuits, labs (gears banked in gbx). The 3 kit asm1 are all there is until automation.
# ~655k (Rory: retire the old sources, the passive provider chests): the Boot module retired
# (fbx, cbx, cix providers; bq2 + the brick furnace: the network holds the 50 bricks O1 needs).








# burner fields (the kit's 10 burner drills). Fuel by ONE coal belt from the coal row, not a
# requester per field (Rory: belts over requesters); cl_cl gives the coal row its first fuel.
fe_dr  = MinerRow<n=4, resource=iron-ore, drill=burner-mining-drill, fuel=coal, inserter=inserter> @(1024, 1105)
fe_sm  = SmelterRow<n=4, recipe=iron-plate, inserter=inserter>      @(1024, 1088)
net fe_ore:  fe_dr -> fe_sm
net fe_pl:   fe_sm -> hub.fe2_in    # S2 (~1029k): st_sm -> fe_pl4 (steel 3.3/min made vs 9.9 used; 2 of 4 burner drills dry); H2b: fe_box -> the hub;  # J1: + the steel row; H0 (~225k): the mall moved to fe_pl4 (electric); burner iron to the network

cu_dr  = MinerRow<n=3, resource=copper-ore, drill=burner-mining-drill, fuel=coal, inserter=inserter> @(1052, 1085)
cu_sm  = SmelterRow<n=2, recipe=copper-plate, inserter=inserter>    @(1054, 1074)
net cu_ore:  cu_dr -> cu_sm
net cu_pl:   cu_sm -> hub.cu2_in    # H2a: cu_box -> the hub;  # I: the makers moved to cu_pl4 (electric)

cl_dr  = MinerRow<n=3, resource=coal, drill=burner-mining-drill, fuel=coal, inserter=inserter> @(1076, 1046)
cl_cl  = Chest<requester, item=coal, request=10> @(1072, 1050)
cl_el  = MinerRow<n=4, resource=coal>   @(1084, 1038)   # C1 (~745k): coal 38/min mined vs 68 burnt; 4 electric drills (+120/min) NE of the burner row
cl_el2 = MinerRow<n=6, resource=coal>   @(1078, 1051)   # C2 (~2460k): 5 of 7 coal drills dry, plastic + boilers short; dense coal x78..88, y50..56
cl_el3 = MinerRow<n=4, resource=coal>   @(1074, 1037)   # C2: coal x74..79, y37..43 W of cl_el
net cl_fuel: cl_cl -> cl_dr
net coal:    cl_dr, cl_el, cl_el2, cl_el3 -> hub.cl_in, cu_dr, cu_sm, fe_dr, fe_sm, fe_sm4, cu_sm4, pl, sb1, sb2
st_cl  = Chest<requester, item=coal, request=20>  @(1013, 1075)   # J1: 1 of the last 4 requesters (adding st_sm to the coal net re-routed all of it: 78 new, 66 taken up; a provider cannot drive a net)
net st_coal: st_cl -> st_sm

# Smelt0 (B: the kit's ore -> plates by the kit roboport) retired ~320k: its 2 requesters freed

# D2: the mall, belt-fed (iron from fe_sm, copper from cu_sm), map 13..33, 58..72, in r1's area.
# The boot's asm1 maker built its 6 machines. Outputs into storage chests with limits.
# S1 (~701k, Rory): outputs into passive providers (they only give to the network; a storage
# chest, even filtered, takes robots' drop-offs, so the auto mall's belts would fly out here).
module Mall size 20x14 {
  port fe_in : in iron-plate   @w6
  port cu_in : in copper-plate @e3
  bx1 = Chest<provider>                         @(6, 0)
  g1  = Assembler<recipe=iron-gear-wheel>       @(1, 2)
  bl  = Assembler<recipe=transport-belt>        @(5, 2)
  ci  = Assembler<recipe=electronic-circuit>    @(10, 2)
  cb  = Assembler<recipe=copper-cable>          @(14, 2)
  ins = Assembler<recipe=inserter>              @(10, 9)
  am  = Assembler<recipe=assembling-machine-1>  @(14, 9)   # H1: asm1 again (the boot was 1 short; 10 drills banked); E: drills; D2: asm1
  bx3 = Chest<provider>                         @(11, 13)
  bx4 = Chest<provider>                         @(15, 13)
  cbx = Chest<provider>                         @(15, 0)
  net fe:   fe_in -> g1, bl, ci, ins, am
  net cu:   cu_in -> cb
  net g1o:  g1 -> bl, ins, am
  net cbo:  cb -> ci
  net cio:  ci -> cbx, ins, am
  net blo:  bl -> bx1
  net ino:  ins -> bx3
  net amo:  am -> bx4
  set bl.out -> bx1:  logistic=transport-belt<300
  set ins.out -> bx3: logistic=inserter<100
  set am.out -> bx4:  logistic=assembling-machine-1<12   # ~372k 4 -> 12: K lays 8 (MilH 5, poles 2, red2)
  set ci.out -> cbx:  logistic=electronic-circuit<100
}
mall = Mall @(1013, 1058)

# E1 (~142k): science, belt-fed beside the mall (map -16..10, 58..72): a gear maker between two
# red makers, red into the 3 spare labs. Room on the east half for green (inserter + belt) later.
module Sci0 size 26x14 {
  port fe_in : in iron-plate   @e2
  port cu_in : in copper-plate @e8
  port rd_out : out automation-science-pack @n3   # K: red to Lab2 (the labs moved there; at w5 it opened onto fe_pl4)
  g1   = Assembler<recipe=iron-gear-wheel>         @(14, 2)
  red1 = Assembler<recipe=automation-science-pack, machine=assembling-machine-2> @(10, 0)
  red2 = Assembler<recipe=automation-science-pack, machine=assembling-machine-2> @(17, 6)   # K: into the freed east half; at (10,4) the copper route never reached it (half-rate red)
  net fe:   fe_in -> g1
  net cu:   cu_in -> red1, red2
  net gm:   g1 -> red1, red2
  net reds: red1, red2 -> rd_out
}
sci = Sci0 @(984, 1058)

# E: electric iron on the field's south half (the old run's D5 spot), its own row into Sci0
# (a new consumer gets its own row). Drills from the mall's am, furnaces from the kit/boot.
fe_el  = MinerRow<n=12, resource=iron-ore>                          @(1024, 1117)   # ~4290k Rory: reposition the starter drills onto the ore left: the south band x24..42, y118..123 (was @1012,1114, all dry)
fe_sm4 = SmelterRow<n=16, recipe=iron-plate, inserter=inserter, machine=steel-furnace> @(1012, 1124)   # I5 (~2112k): steel furnaces, the ore belt backed up. I2 (~885k): 12 -> 16 for fe_el2   # 1122: a drill had no pole spot
# I2 (~885k): a 2nd electric iron row on the field's rich east (x34..45, y99..105, ~75k): 4
# drills (~120 ore/min) into fe_sm4, grown 12 -> 16 east along its coal belt (a new row's coal
# couldn't branch, and x48..59 sat on the coal + copper-ore belts). Iron was 239 made / 227 used.
fe_el2 = MinerRow<n=4, resource=iron-ore>                           @(1040, 1101)   # ~4290k: the east strip x40..46, y100..112 (was @1034,1099, dry)
fe_el3 = MinerRow<n=6, resource=iron-ore>                           @(1012, 1102)   # ~4290k: the west strip x12..22, y102..112 (was @1024,1097, dry)   # I3 (~1357k): 4 of fe_el's 8 drills and all 4 burners ran dry; free ore x24..32, y97..103
fe_el4 = MinerRow<n=10, resource=iron-ore>                          @(1025, 1110)   # I4 (~2096k): free ore x25..39, y110..116; 21 dead drills
net fe_ore4:  fe_el, fe_el2, fe_el3, fe_el4 -> fe_sm4
net fe_pl4:   fe_sm4 -> sci.fe_in, grn.fe_in, mall.fe_in, hub.fe_in, int.fe_in, blue.ir_in, st_sm, gw3, pp3, acid, bat, ci4, ci5   # ~4490k back as it stands (epl's branch to blue.ir_in didn't join; a forced epl reroute was the 40-min route): the moved fe_el* drills feed fe_sm4 again; ~655k: fe_box4 (a far provider) -> the hub;  # H0: + mall (the belt runs past its port at x10)

# G (~184k): green science, its own makers (cable -> circuits -> inserters; gears -> belts), two
# green makers, packs south to Sci0's labs. Map -6..24, 40..54 (north of Sci0 and the mall).
module Grn0 size 30x14 {
  port fe_in  : in iron-plate   @s3
  port cu_in  : in copper-plate @s9
  port gr_out : out logistic-science-pack @s26
  cb  = Assembler<recipe=copper-cable>            @(1, 1)
  ci  = Assembler<recipe=electronic-circuit>      @(5, 1)
  im  = Assembler<recipe=inserter>                @(9, 1)
  g2  = Assembler<recipe=iron-gear-wheel>         @(13, 1)
  bm  = Assembler<recipe=transport-belt>          @(17, 1)
  gn1 = Assembler<recipe=logistic-science-pack, machine=assembling-machine-2>   @(11, 6)
  gn2 = Assembler<recipe=logistic-science-pack, machine=assembling-machine-2>   @(17, 6)
  net fe:   fe_in -> ci, im, g2, bm
  net cu:   cu_in -> cb
  net cab:  cb -> ci
  net cir:  ci -> im
  net gr:   g2 -> im, bm
  net insn: im -> gn1, gn2
  net beln: bm -> gn1, gn2
  lanes insn | beln
  net out:  gn1, gn2 -> gr_out
}
grn = Grn0 @(994, 1040)
net grn_s: grn.gr_out -> labs.gr_in, lab3   # K: green to Lab2

# I (pasted ~274k; drafted to wait until >=4 splitters and ~150 belts are banked: taking up cu_pl cuts the
# mall's copper until cu_pl4 stands, and the splitters need the mall's circuits): electric copper (the burners give ~45/min to three makers): 8 drills on the patch's
# west half, 12 furnaces south of it, its own belt north to the mall, Sci0 and Grn0.
cu_el  = MinerRow<n=8, resource=copper-ore>                          @(1048, 1091)
cu_sm4 = SmelterRow<n=10, recipe=copper-plate, inserter=inserter>    @(1048, 1108)
net cu_ore4: cu_el -> cu_sm4
net cu_pl4:  cu_sm4 -> mall.cu_in, sci.cu_in, grn.cu_in, hub.cu_in, int.cu_in, blue.cu_in, bat, cb4, cb5   # ~655k H2b: the rest to the hub
# stone (nothing mines it; furnaces need it): two electric drills into a box, for a furnace maker
st_el  = MinerRow<n=2, resource=stone>   @(1044, 1055)
# BR1 (~2220k): nothing put bricks in the network (bk feeds MilH's walls only), so the mall
# could not make steel furnaces. A brick row by the hub, out to a provider in the hub zone.
br_sm  = SmelterRow<n=6, recipe=stone-brick, inserter=inserter>   @(1050, 1006)
brx    = Chest<provider, limit=4>                                 @(1040, 1000)
net brko: br_sm -> brx
brq    = Chest<requester, item=coal, request=50>                  @(1040, 1003)   # hub zone; adding br_sm to the coal net re-laid it whole (176 belts, by the boilers): J1's lesson
net brc:  brq -> br_sm
# BR2 (~2250k): 4 of 6 brick furnaces sat short of stone (st_el's 2 drills feed hub + MilH too):
# more stone drills on the free ore between the x48 and x53 belts, on st_out (a SmelterRow takes 2 belts).
st_el2 = MinerRow<n=2, resource=stone>   @(1049, 1053)
st_el3 = MinerRow<n=2, resource=stone>   @(1049, 1061)
set br_sm.out -> brx: logistic=stone-brick<1000
net st_out: st_el, st_el2, st_el3 -> hub.st_in, mil.st_in, br_sm   # H2a: st_box -> the hub

# J1 (~293k): steel off the burner iron (fe_pl, ~60/min: 4 furnaces), north of fe_sm in free
# ground (map 18..26, 77..80), into a box for the network (poles, Mil's piercing rounds later).
st_sm  = SmelterRow<n=7, recipe=steel-plate, inserter=inserter>   @(1015, 1074)   # S3 (~1101k): 4 -> 7: blue's 2nd engine maker sat short of steel (blue 3.8/min, labs missing packs)
net stl_out: st_sm -> hub.sl_in, mil.sl_in, blue.sl_in, en3, frm   # H2a: st_bx -> the hub

# K (~330k): military science by the hub's rule (requesters in one module, the rest by belt):
# 3 requesters feed firearm mags + grenades (iron, coal), piercing rounds (copper, steel) and the
# brick furnace (stone, coal: a furnace on its own requester, or it smelts the iron); packs go by
# belt east into Sci0's labs (their 3rd input). Map -42..-19, 58..68.
module MilH size 22x10 {
  port mi_out : out military-science-pack @s3   # straight down into labs.mi_in (at e5 it sat on fe_pl4)
  # H3a (~796k): steel + stone by belt from their furnaces/drills; iron, coal, copper stay requested
  # (the iron/copper/coal mains won't branch here: the next step moves MilH by the hub)
  rq1 = Chest<requester, item="iron-plate,coal", request=20>      @(4, 1)
  rq2 = Chest<requester, item="copper-plate", request=20>         @(11, 1)
  rq3 = Chest<requester, item="coal", request=20>                 @(18, 1)
  port sl_in : in steel-plate  @n12
  port st_in : in stone        @n19
  fm  = Assembler<recipe=firearm-magazine>        @(0, 0)
  gr  = Assembler<recipe=grenade, machine=assembling-machine-2, modules=speed-module> @(3, 3)   # ~504k: right under rq1 (direct); at (5,4) its iron+coal shared a belt that filled with coal
  pr  = Assembler<recipe=piercing-rounds-magazine, machine=assembling-machine-2> @(7, 0)
  bk  = Furnace<recipe=stone-brick, machine=steel-furnace> @(18, 3)   # M9 (~1909k): bricks capped walls -> mil packs (stone furnace 0.31/s, need ~0.75)   # ~452k: right under rq3 (direct); at (19,4) a belt took stone+coal, filled with stone, the furnace never got fuel
  wl  = Assembler<recipe=stone-wall>              @(14, 4)   # ~452k: 1 W so bk -> wl and wl -> mx stay direct
  mx  = Assembler<recipe=military-science-pack, machine=assembling-machine-2, modules=speed-module> @(10, 6)   # M8 (~1891k): lab3 used more mil packs than made
  ab  = Chest<provider>                           @(8, 4)   # A1 (~706k, Rory): the turrets' ammo comes from here, not the hub
  net r1:  rq1 -> fm, gr
  net r2:  rq2 -> pr
  net si:  sl_in -> pr
  net r3:  rq3 -> bk
  net ti:  st_in -> bk
  net fmo: fm -> pr
  net bko: bk -> wl
  net pro: pr -> mx, ab
  net gro: gr -> mx
  net wlo: wl -> mx
  net out: mx -> mi_out
  set pr.out -> ab: logistic=piercing-rounds-magazine<150   # ~993k 50 -> 150: biters took 8 of 11 turrets
}
mil = MilH @(961, 1058)   # map -39..-18: rq1 inside r3's logistic square, clear of the x-17 belt
# B1: net mi_s (mil.mi_out -> labs.mi_in) off until a 2nd lab row; MilH banks its packs

# K: Lab2, every lab in one roomy module of its own on the free west ground (map -42..-20,
# 71..87): red from Sci0, green from Grn0, military from MilH, each on its own belt.
module Lab2 size 22x16 {
  port rd_in : in automation-science-pack @e3
  port gr_in : in logistic-science-pack   @e8
  port bl_in : in chemical-science-pack   @n6    # B1 (~940k): blue in military's place (a LabRow takes 3 belts); military waits for a 2nd row
  row = LabRow<n=6>                       @(2, 6)   # ~972k: 5 -> 6 (labs were the limit: 10 packs/min used of 18 red + 15 green)
  net r: rd_in -> row
  net g: gr_in -> row
  net b: bl_in -> row
}
labs = Lab2 @(958, 1071)
net red_s: sci.rd_out -> labs.rd_in, lab3

# L (pole shop) retired ~533k: the auto mall keeps medium poles 40; its requester goes to O1


# M2 (~506k): the AUTO MALL v0 (automall/gen_mall_v0.py: no selector, round-robin pick; tested
# in fk sim ~480-520k: stocked gears, pipe, then circuits/cable by itself). Its roboport IS r1
# (map -12,26): the mall's frame starts 9 tiles above it, on the free ground north of r1.
automall = Literal<file="mall-v0.json"> @(1006, 997)   # H1 (~585k, Rory: all the logistic chests in one small area, where the storage chests are, off the ore): on the kit roboport (map 6,6), by the kit's 6 storage chests; was on r1 (map -12,17), 70-110 tiles from its plates

# H2 (~603k, Rory: "the logistic chests that matter are all the provider chests scattered about
# the base"; "any logistic chest not in the hub zone is clearly a high cost"): THE HUB, beside the
# mall (kit roboport) and the kit's storage chests, off the ore (map 15..28, -3..2). Each line
# belts in to a box of its own; the old boxes are taken up and their plates hauled here.
# H2a: burner copper, stone, steel. H2b: the iron mains (fe_pl4, burner fe_pl) and cu_pl4.
module Hub size 14x6 {
  port fe_in  : in iron-plate   @s1
  port fe2_in : in iron-plate   @s3
  port cu_in  : in copper-plate @s5
  port cu2_in : in copper-plate @s7
  port st_in  : in stone        @s9
  port sl_in  : in steel-plate  @s12
  port cl_in  : in coal         @n11
  fe = Chest<storage, item=iron-plate> @(2, 1)
  cu = Chest<storage, item=copper-plate> @(6, 1)
  st = Chest<storage, item=stone> @(9, 1)
  sl = Chest<storage, item=steel-plate, limit=5> @(12, 1)   # L7 (~1406k): steel ate ~130 iron/min for ~7 used; the cap backs st_sm up so iron reaches int + blue
  cl = Chest<storage, item=coal> @(11, 4)
  net f1: fe_in -> fe
  net f2: fe2_in -> fe
  net c1: cu_in -> cu
  net k1: cl_in -> cl
  net c2: cu2_in -> cu
  net s1: st_in -> st
  net l1: sl_in -> sl
}
hub = Hub @(1015, 997)

# I1 (~713k, Rory: supply gears and green circuits to the network so the mall's one assembler
# makes buildings): belt-fed gear + circuit makers N of the hub (map 18..32, -14..-5, inside the kit roboport), their
# products into filtered storage boxes (passive providers wait on construction-robotics).
module Int size 15x10 {
  port fe_in : in iron-plate   @s3
  port cu_in : in copper-plate @s10
  gw  = Assembler<recipe=iron-gear-wheel>    @(0, 1)
  cb1 = Assembler<recipe=copper-cable>       @(5, 1)
  cb2 = Assembler<recipe=copper-cable>       @(5, 5)
  ci  = Assembler<recipe=electronic-circuit> @(9, 3)
  gb  = Chest<storage, item=iron-gear-wheel>    @(1, 6)
  cx  = Chest<storage, item=electronic-circuit> @(14, 4)
  net fi: fe_in -> gw, ci
  net ci2: cu_in -> cb1, cb2
  net cbl: cb1, cb2 -> ci
  port ci_out : out electronic-circuit @n12
  net gwo: gw -> gb
  net cio: ci -> cx, ci_out
  set gw.out -> gb: logistic=iron-gear-wheel<300
  set ci.out -> cx: logistic=electronic-circuit<300
}
int = Int @(1018, 986)   # map 18..32, -14..-5

# O1a (~616k): the pumpjacks alone, ahead of the oil block: oil-processing is a TRIGGER tech (mine
# 1 crude), and it gates sulfur -> explosives -> land mines (the biters hit the base from the
# south now). No net yet: each fills its own tank, which is the mining that counts.
pj1  = Pumpjack<n=1>                            @(1005, 989)
pj2  = Pumpjack<n=1>                            @(1010, 989)
pj3  = Pumpjack<n=1>                            @(1015, 989)


# O1 (draft ~532k): the OIL BLOCK -> land mines (Rory: landmines are the defense). Wells at map
# 6.5/11.5/16.5,-9.5; water's east shore at x -12 (y -53..-48). Inside the plant roboport's
# logistic square (map -47..3, -51..-1). O1 (~780k): coal and steel by belt from HubO, two hub
# requesters N of the mall (Rory: the hub rule), one belt per machine (no shared belt: MilH's lesson).
module HubO size 8x4 {
  port c_out : out coal        @n2
  port s_out : out steel-plate @n6
  hc = Chest<requester, item=coal, request=50>        @(2, 2)
  hs = Chest<requester, item=steel-plate, request=50> @(6, 2)
  net c: hc -> c_out
  net s: hs -> s_out
}
hubo = HubO @(996, 992)   # map -4..3, -8..-5: by the mall and the kit's storage chests
ref  = Refinery<recipe=advanced-oil-processing>    @(1003, 975)
osp  = OffshorePump<rate=1200/s>                @(989, 950, rot 3)
sul  = ChemPlant<recipe=sulfur>                 @(995, 965)
exp  = ChemPlant<recipe=explosives>             @(991, 965)
lm   = Assembler<recipe=land-mine, machine=assembling-machine-2> @(991, 969)   # ~3560k: asm1 was the campaign's limit (exp sat full); asm2 = 36/min
mbx  = Chest<provider, limit=30>                @(995, 970)
net crude: pj1, pj2, pj3 -> ref
net petro: ref, lcr -> sul, pl
net water: osp -> sul, exp, hcr, lcr, acid, ref   # R1b: advanced-oil-processing takes water too
net sulf:  sul -> exp, blue.su_in, acid
net expl:  exp -> lm
net exc:   hubo.c_out -> exp
net stl:   hubo.s_out -> lm
net mines: lm -> mbx
set lm.out -> mbx: logistic=land-mine<600   # ~3560k: was 200, which capped the campaign's stock

# B1 (~940k): BLUE SCIENCE. One pack maker (asm2, ~9 packs/min) on 2 engine + 2 advanced-circuit
# makers (asm2), its own plastic plant, cable and pipe makers. N of Int on clear ground (map
# 12..37, -40..-27). Petroleum piped from the refinery, sulfur belted from O1's plant, gears and
# circuits belted from Int; coal, steel, iron, copper off their main lines where they end at the
# hub (requester chests are locked until construction-robotics); the packs on one belt to Lab2.
module Blue size 32x16 {
  port pb_in : in plastic-bar        @w3
  port cu_in : in copper-plate       @w11
  port ci_in : in electronic-circuit @s7
  port ir_in : in iron-plate         @s15
  port sl_in : in steel-plate        @s21
  port su_in : in sulfur             @n27
  port bl_out : out chemical-science-pack @e8
  cb  = Assembler<recipe=copper-cable, machine=assembling-machine-2>          @(1, 9)   # B3: asm2, it feeds ci too
  ci  = Assembler<recipe=electronic-circuit, machine=assembling-machine-2>    @(23, 11)  # B3 (~1496k): Blue's own green circuits (int's ci starved ac1/ac2)
  ac1 = Assembler<recipe=advanced-circuit, machine=assembling-machine-2>      @(7, 2)
  ac2 = Assembler<recipe=advanced-circuit, machine=assembling-machine-2>      @(7, 9)
  gw  = Assembler<recipe=iron-gear-wheel>                                     @(14, 11)
  pp  = Assembler<recipe=pipe>                                                @(18, 11)
  en1 = Assembler<recipe=engine-unit, machine=assembling-machine-2>           @(15, 3)
  en2 = Assembler<recipe=engine-unit, machine=assembling-machine-2>           @(20, 5)
  bl  = Assembler<recipe=chemical-science-pack, machine=assembling-machine-2, modules=speed-module> @(27, 7)   # B5 (~2490k): nuclear-power takes 800 blue
  bl2 = Assembler<recipe=chemical-science-pack, machine=assembling-machine-2, modules=speed-module> @(27, 2)   # B2 (~1120k): 1 pack maker capped blue at 3.75/min
  net plo: pb_in -> ac1, ac2
  net cu:  cu_in -> cb
  net cbo: cb -> ac1, ac2, ci
  net ci:  ci_in, ci -> ac1, ac2
  net ir:  ir_in -> pp, gw, ci
  net ppo: pp -> en1, en2
  net gwo: gw -> en1, en2
  net sl:  sl_in -> en1, en2
  net aco: ac1, ac2 -> bl, bl2
  net eno: en1, en2 -> bl, bl2
  net su:  su_in -> bl, bl2
  net out: bl, bl2 -> bl_out
}
blue = Blue @(1012, 958)   # map 12..43, -42..-27

pl   = ChemPlant<recipe=plastic-bar>           @(1008, 968)   # B1: plastic beside the refinery (a module port takes no fluid)
net bpl: pl -> blue.pb_in, ac4, ac5, ac6
net bci: int.ci_out -> blue.ci_in, ee, frm, ac4, bm.gc   # P1: + the belt mall's splitters
net bpk: blue.bl_out -> labs.bl_in

# R1 (~1175k): ROBOT PARTS north of Blue (map 0..42, -53..-44), ~20 tiles from the refinery.
hcr  = ChemPlant<recipe=heavy-oil-cracking>   @(1000, 947)
lcr  = ChemPlant<recipe=light-oil-cracking>   @(1006, 947)
lub  = ChemPlant<recipe=lubricant>            @(1012, 947)
acid = ChemPlant<recipe=sulfuric-acid>        @(1018, 947)
bat  = ChemPlant<recipe=battery>              @(1024, 947)
gw3  = Assembler<recipe=iron-gear-wheel>      @(1030, 951)
pp3  = Assembler<recipe=pipe>                 @(1034, 951)
en3  = Assembler<recipe=engine-unit, machine=assembling-machine-2>          @(1030, 946)
ee   = Assembler<recipe=electric-engine-unit, machine=assembling-machine-2> @(1035, 946)
frm  = Assembler<recipe=flying-robot-frame, machine=assembling-machine-2>   @(1040, 946)
fbx  = Chest<provider, limit=2>               @(1044, 947)
net heavy: ref -> lub, hcr
net light: ref, hcr -> lcr
net acidn: acid -> bat, ab
# U0 (~2370k): acid barrels for the uranium trigger. Empty barrels go into ab by an item-request
# proxy (no requester chests: logistic-system needs space science); full ones out to abp.
ab   = Assembler<recipe=sulfuric-acid-barrel, machine=assembling-machine-2> @(1032, 934)
abp  = Chest<provider, limit=1>                                            @(1036, 935)
net abo2: ab -> abp
set ab.out -> abp: logistic=sulfuric-acid-barrel<20
net lubn:  lub -> ee
net gw3o:  gw3 -> en3
net pp3o:  pp3 -> en3
net en3o:  en3 -> ee
net een:   ee -> frm
net batn:  bat -> frm, bbx
# P4 (~2035k): batteries to the network for accumulators (the mall)
bbx  = Chest<provider, limit=1>               @(1024, 951)
set bat.out -> bbx: logistic=battery<200
net frms:  frm -> fbx
set frm.out -> fbx: logistic=flying-robot-frame<100

# A2 (~1604k): advanced circuits TO THE NETWORK for the mall (speed modules, roboports, beacons):
# all of Blue's go to its pack makers. Map 37..45, -15..-8, beside Int (r5's logistic area).
cb4  = Assembler<recipe=copper-cable, machine=assembling-machine-2>     @(1041, 985)
ac4  = Assembler<recipe=advanced-circuit, machine=assembling-machine-2> @(1037, 985)
abx  = Chest<provider, limit=6>                                         @(1038, 983)   # A2b: at y -17, inside r5's logistic area (y -13 was its edge; at -9.5 robots never saw it)
net cb4o: cb4 -> ac4, ci4
# A3 (~1802k): ac4 starved of green circuits (bci is shared with blue, ee, frm): its own maker.
ci4  = Assembler<recipe=electronic-circuit, machine=assembling-machine-2> @(1045, 985)
net ci4o: ci4 -> ac4
# A4b (~2415k, Rory: lines, not single makers): ac4 alone (~7.5/min) starves roboports, provider
# chests, bulk inserters. Plastic sits in surplus (54), so no 2nd plastic plant (A4's coal belt
# to pl2 failed the route): ac5, ac6 share bpl; cb5 + ci5 feed them.
ac5  = Assembler<recipe=advanced-circuit, machine=assembling-machine-2> @(1049, 985)
ac6  = Assembler<recipe=advanced-circuit, machine=assembling-machine-2> @(1057, 985)
cb5  = Assembler<recipe=copper-cable, machine=assembling-machine-2>     @(1061, 985)
ci5  = Assembler<recipe=electronic-circuit, machine=assembling-machine-2> @(1053, 985)   # between ac5 and ac6: hands to both
net cb5o: cb5 -> ac5, ac6, ci5
net ci5o: ci5 -> ac5, ac6
net abo:  ac4, ac5, ac6 -> abx
set ac4.out -> abx: logistic=advanced-circuit<1000   # ~2175k Rory: 50 was one roboport; 1000 lets the mall batch 20

# L3 (~1712k): a 2nd lab row for MILITARY packs (Lab2 takes red, green, blue: a LabRow takes 3
# belts). Map -40..-23, 87..94, below Lab2. MilH has banked 153 packs; shooting-speed-3 and
# physical-damage-3 need them.
lab3 = LabRow<n=6>                          @(958, 1090)
net mi_s: mil.mi_out -> lab3

# P1 (~1730k): STEAM POWER. The kit's reactor runs 1 heat exchanger (10 MW) and the accumulators sat
# empty (labs low_power). Nuclear-power is far (uranium); solar-energy queued first. 2 boilers + 4
# engines (3.6 MW) on the lake's east shore (map -7..10, -79..-58), coal off the coal net.
osp2 = OffshorePump<rate=1200/s>               @(993, 938, rot 3)
sb1  = Boiler<fuel=coal>                       @(995, 934)
sb2  = Boiler<fuel=coal>                       @(1003, 934)
se1  = SteamEngine                             @(995, 921)
se2  = SteamEngine                             @(995, 926)
se3  = SteamEngine                             @(1003, 921)
se4  = SteamEngine                             @(1003, 926)
net swater: osp2 -> sb1, sb2
net steam:  sb1, sb2 -> se1, se2, se3, se4

# E3b (~2680k): the real base's first linear array on the east iron (patch x274..306, y-70..-40;
# lab game/eiron.fk 96% of 900/min). Two 16-drill rows on the dense core, 12 FurnacePair cells
# (24 electric furnaces) west of it; the plates belt west into the hub zone until the east has
# its own makers (then re-point epl). Power: ~7 MW (N1 gave 30 MW more).
ei_a   = MinerRow<n=16, resource=iron-ore>   @(1278, 936)   # map 278,-64
ei_b   = MinerRow<n=16, resource=iron-ore>   @(1278, 946)   # map 278,-54
ei_col = Stack<cell=FurnacePair, n=12>       @(1258, 928)   # map 258..271, -72..-36
ebx    = Chest<provider, limit=8>            @(1045, 998)   # hub zone, map 45,-2
net eoa: ei_a -> ei_col.oa_in
net eob: ei_b -> ei_col.ob_in
net epl: ei_col.pl_out -> bm.fe, ebx   # ~4490k: back to the standing route; P1 (~3260k): the belt mall takes its iron on the way to ebx

# P1 (~3260k, Rory: "a 3x2 belt factory that settles you on tier 1 and 2 belts fully"): BeltMall
# (beltmall.fk, lab-tested ~3225k) on the open ground E of the dense base, map 68..108, -1..21, by
# epl's belt (y-4). Its 6 providers extend the hub zone east (the east builds fetch belts here).
# Circuits on int's belt (net bci; requester chests need logistic-system): P3 belts more later.
bm     = BeltMall2                                                  @(1068, 999)   # P1b (~3415k): Rory's tight 3x2 pattern, 27x15 (map 68..95, -1..14)

# E6 (~2870k): the REAL BASE's smelting on the big east field (wave 2 cleared it; e12..e14 cover
# it). Iron: two 16-drill rows on the dense core (x530..556, y-84..-54) + 12 FurnacePair W of the
# patch; copper: the same with CopperPair (lab ecopper.fk ~870/min). Plates go W into plain chests
# in the factory district (x440..500) until the blue line there takes the belts.
fe2_a   = MinerRow<n=16, resource=iron-ore>     @(1530, 918)   # map 530,-82
fe2_b   = MinerRow<n=16, resource=iron-ore>     @(1530, 928)   # map 530,-72
fe2_col = Stack<cell=FurnacePair, n=12>         @(1507, 900)   # map 507..520, -100..-64
fe2_box = Chest<plain>                          @(1480, 960)   # map 480,-40 (district)
net fe2a: fe2_a -> fe2_col.oa_in
net fe2b: fe2_b -> fe2_col.ob_in
net fe2p: fe2_col.pl_out -> s5_gear.in_in, s5_circ.wi_in, s5_circ.ei_in, s5_grn.fe_in, b5_st.in_in, b5_gear, b5_pipe, b5_circ.wi_in, b5_circ.ei_in, fe2_box   # P5a; P5b: + the blue line: through the science district
cu2_a   = MinerRow<n=16, resource=copper-ore>   @(1528, 848)   # map 528,-152
cu2_b   = MinerRow<n=16, resource=copper-ore>   @(1528, 858)   # map 528,-142
cu2_col = Stack<cell=CopperPair, n=12>          @(1505, 830)   # map 505..518, -170..-134
net cu2a: cu2_a -> cu2_col.oa_in
net cu2b: cu2_b -> cu2_col.ob_in
net cu2p: cu2_col.pl_out -> s5_circ.cu_in, s5_red.c_in, b5_circ.cu_in, b5_cabl   # P5a; P5b: + the blue line. ~4480k cu2_box gone: its corner (480,-130) is cliffs; the row runs south at x499 and along y-128.5 (helpers/cu2detour.lua, fk adopt)

# P4 (~3740k, Rory: "belt in coal from the north east huge patch, and pipe in oil, both to a location
# somewhere in the middle"): the CHEM BLOCK on the lake's W shore (map 392..435, 168..188; the
# middle ~290,40 has no water). Crude from the SE wells (8 pumpjacks, x167..193, y218..245,
# ~3.5M) piped ~230 tiles; coal from a 4-drill row on the east coal (map 386,-152, 5.3M) belted
# ~330 tiles south; water from the lake. Basic oil processing (no water, no cracking): 4
# refineries ~36 petroleum/s -> 2 plastic plants (~150/min with 75 coal/min) + 1 sulfur plant.
# Plastic + sulfur into providers for now (TEMPORARY: P5's science line belts them later).
c4_pj1 = Pumpjack<n=1> @(1182, 1218)
c4_pj2 = Pumpjack<n=1> @(1185, 1233)
c4_pj3 = Pumpjack<n=1> @(1175, 1235)
c4_pj4 = Pumpjack<n=1> @(1167, 1238)
c4_pj5 = Pumpjack<n=1> @(1191, 1237)
c4_pj6 = Pumpjack<n=1> @(1175, 1240)
c4_pj7 = Pumpjack<n=1> @(1185, 1239)
c4_pj8 = Pumpjack<n=1> @(1172, 1243)
c4_r1  = Refinery<recipe=basic-oil-processing>   @(1392, 1170)
c4_r2  = Refinery<recipe=basic-oil-processing>   @(1399, 1170)
c4_r3  = Refinery<recipe=basic-oil-processing>   @(1406, 1170)
c4_r4  = Refinery<recipe=basic-oil-processing>   @(1413, 1170)
c4_pl1 = ChemPlant<recipe=plastic-bar>           @(1394, 1180)
c4_pl2 = ChemPlant<recipe=plastic-bar>           @(1400, 1180)
c4_su  = ChemPlant<recipe=sulfur>                @(1410, 1180)
c4_osp = OffshorePump<rate=1200/s>               @(1435, 1177, rot 1)   # ~4470k Rory moved it one tile onto the water's edge
c4_cm  = MinerRow<n=4, resource=coal>            @(1386, 848)    # map 386,-152
c4_pb  = Chest<provider, limit=4>                @(1396, 1186)
c4_sb  = Chest<provider, limit=2>                @(1412, 1186)
net c4_crude: c4_pj1, c4_pj2, c4_pj3, c4_pj4, c4_pj5, c4_pj6, c4_pj7, c4_pj8 -> c4_r1, c4_r2, c4_r3, c4_r4
net c4_pet:   c4_r1, c4_r2, c4_r3, c4_r4 -> c4_pl1, c4_pl2, c4_su
net c4_wat:   c4_osp -> c4_su
net c4_coal:  c4_cm -> c4_pl1, c4_pl2
net c4_plo:   c4_pl1, c4_pl2 -> c4_pb, b5_adv.p_in   # P5b
net c4_suo:   c4_su -> c4_sb, b5_chem.su_in   # P5b

# P5a (~3900k, Rory: "get your new base red green blue science up, so you can really push towards
# space"): the SCIENCE DISTRICT on the open ground W of fe2_col (map 446..483, -104..-60), cells
# lab-tested in game/scilab.fk (~3895k: red 36/min, green 31/min). Iron from fe2p, copper from cu2p
# (their boxes stay as the ends). North row: gears + circuits; south row: red, green, labs. Blue
# packs (labs.b_in) come with P5b's blue line.
s5_gear = Stack<cell=GearCell, n=4>     @(1446, 896)    # map 446,-104
s5_circ = CircuitCell                   @(1456, 896)    # map 456..479, -104..-96
s5_red  = Stack<cell=RedCell2, n=4>     @(1446, 920)    # map 446,-80
s5_grn  = Stack<cell=GreenCell, n=4>    @(1458, 916)    # map 458,-84
s5_labs = Stack<cell=LabCell3, n=6>     @(1476, 916)    # map 476,-84
net s5_gw: s5_gear.out_out -> s5_red.g_in, s5_grn.g_in
net s5_gc: s5_circ.wo_out, s5_circ.eo_out -> s5_grn.c_in
net s5_rp: s5_red.p_out -> larea.r_in   # ~4240k: to the lab area (was s5_labs.r_in)
net s5_gp: s5_grn.p_out -> larea.g_in   # ~4240k: to the lab area (was s5_labs.g_in)

# P5b (~4005k, Rory: new-base red green BLUE science): the lab-tested blue line (blueline.fk, 174/174
# nets) south of the science district, map 400..496, -34..12, on fe2's spare iron, cu2's copper, P4's plastic and sulfur by belt; the packs go north to s5_labs.
# fe3 (an own iron column, 24 electric furnaces = 120 adv circuits) waits for b5_acb's circuits;
# until then the line runs on fe2p's spare iron (fe2p is re-pointed through b5 below).

b5_circ = CircuitCell                                                     @(1400, 978)
b5_gear = Assembler<recipe=iron-gear-wheel, machine=assembling-machine-2> @(1484, 970)
b5_pipe = Assembler<recipe=pipe, machine=assembling-machine-2>            @(1488, 970)
b5_cabl = Assembler<recipe=copper-cable, machine=assembling-machine-2>    @(1492, 970)
b5_adv  = Stack<cell=AdvCircuitCell2, n=8>      @(1430, 988)   # 8 not 6: the spare goes to b5_acb (roboports)
b5_eng  = Stack<cell=EngineCell, n=7>           @(1446, 988)
b5_chem = Stack<cell=ChemCell2, n=8>            @(1462, 988)
b5_st   = Stack<cell=SteelCell, n=4>            @(1477, 988)
b5_acb  = Chest<provider, limit=5>              @(1466, 983)   # north of b5_chem, where the a lane leaves; adv circuits for the mall's roboports (temporary, outside the hub)

net b5_gc: b5_circ.wo_out, b5_circ.eo_out -> b5_adv.g_in
net b5_cb: b5_cabl -> b5_adv.cb_in
net b5_st2 items steel-plate:     b5_st.out_out -> b5_eng.sg_in
net b5_gw  items iron-gear-wheel: b5_gear -> b5_eng.sg_in
lanes b5_st2 | b5_gw
net b5_pi: b5_pipe -> b5_eng.pi_in
net b5_en: b5_eng.en_out -> b5_chem.e_in
net b5_ac: b5_adv.ac_out -> b5_chem.a_in, b5_acb
net b5_bp: b5_chem.bp_out -> larea.b_in   # ~4240k: to the lab area (was s5_labs.b_in)
dnp c4_pb, c4_sb, b5_acb, s5_labs   # do not populate: laid out, not built

# LAB AREA (~4240k, Rory: labs apart from any factory, room for many more than 6): his second
# daisy-chain design (game/labrowb.fk, lab-tested: a 6-row stack, all 18 labs got red, green and
# blue). ~4480k (Rory: "everything in the real base should be extensively subdivided"): a SEALED
# region, game/labarea.fk (lab-tested: 72/72 nets in 12 s, all 36 labs got 3 packs): his sample
# (88..103,-104..-87) is labsW, labsE beside it (6 rows each); packs in at the east edge (e20 b,
# e23 g, e26 r), split in the 14-row band above his block A (y-72). Frame map 88..121, -104..-73.
larea = LabArea @(1088, 896)

# (the POLE SHOP drafted ~4285k is dropped ~4480k: the skip mall keeps 150 poles by itself)
e16 = Roboport @(1458, 1034)   # map 460,36: the P4 -> b5 plastic/sulfur belts (L-inf 50 to e8)
e17 = Roboport @(1123, 918)    # map 125,-80: labsE's east edge (44 to 100,-36)
e18 = Roboport @(1128, 1148)   # map 130,150: the SE-well pole line (50 to 80,150)
e19 = Roboport @(1160, 1188)   # map 162,190: the same, to 210,225
e20 = Roboport @(1398, 1160)   # map 400,162: round the chem lake's W side (37 to 440,130)
e21 = Roboport @(1414, 1204)   # map 416,206: joins the chem block's island (24 to 440,215)
